/S /P
/E (The period, also known as the full stop, is a simple yet powerful punctuation mark that signifies the end of a sentence. Its primary function is to provide a clear and definitive stop, allowing readers to process the information presented before moving on to the next idea. In addition to marking the end of a declarative statement, the period can also be used in abbreviations and initials. Despite its small size, the period plays a crucial role in shaping the flow and rhythm of written language, ensuring clarity and coherence in communication.)
